{"assets":["/statement-assets/cc419bd03f46fd6e83cf366b8c7164006bf66b4ce717e57a575a3f6b282e0ae3.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1136","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Nastya Is Transposing Matrices"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Nastya came to her informatics lesson, and her teacher who is, by the way, a little bit famous here gave her the following task."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Two matrices $$$A$$$ and $$$B$$$ are given, each of them has size $$$n \\times m$$$. Nastya can perform the following operation to matrix $$$A$$$ unlimited number of times: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" take any square "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"square submatrix"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$A$$$ and transpose it (i.e. the element of the submatrix which was in the $$$i$$$-th row and $$$j$$$-th column of the submatrix will be in the $$$j$$$-th row and $$$i$$$-th column after transposing, and the transposed submatrix itself will keep its place in the matrix $$$A$$$). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Nastya's task is to check whether it is possible to transform the matrix $$$A$$$ to the matrix $$$B$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/cc419bd03f46fd6e83cf366b8c7164006bf66b4ce717e57a575a3f6b282e0ae3.png"},"kind":"image"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example of the operation"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As it may require a lot of operations, you are asked to answer this question for Nastya."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"square submatrix"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of matrix $$$M$$$ is a matrix which consist of all elements which comes from one of the rows with indeces $$$x, x+1, \\dots, x+k-1$$$ of matrix $$$M$$$ and comes from one of the columns with indeces $$$y, y+1, \\dots, y+k-1$$$ of matrix $$$M$$$. $$$k$$$ is the size of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"square submatrix"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". In other words, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"square submatrix"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the set of elements of source matrix which form a solid square (i.e. without holes)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ separated by space ($$$1 \\leq n, m \\leq 500$$$) — the numbers of rows and columns in $$$A$$$ and $$$B$$$ respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$n$$$ lines contains $$$m$$$ integers, the $$$j$$$-th number in the $$$i$$$-th of these lines denotes the $$$j$$$-th element of the $$$i$$$-th row of the matrix $$$A$$$ ($$$1 \\leq A_{ij} \\leq 10^{9}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$n$$$ lines contains $$$m$$$ integers, the $$$j$$$-th number in the $$$i$$$-th of these lines denotes the $$$j$$$-th element of the $$$i$$$-th row of the matrix $$$B$$$ ($$$1 \\leq B_{ij} \\leq 10^{9}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) if it is possible to transform $$$A$$$ to $$$B$$$ and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can print each letter in any case (upper or lower)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 2\n1 1\n6 1\n1 6\n1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2 2\n4 4\n4 5\n5 4\n4 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nNO"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 3\n1 2 3\n4 5 6\n7 8 9\n1 4 7\n2 5 6\n3 8 9\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the third example. The matrix $$$A$$$ initially looks as follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$ \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3\\\\ 4 & 5 & 6\\\\ 7 & 8 & 9 \\end{bmatrix} $$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then we choose the whole matrix as transposed submatrix and it becomes"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$ \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 4 & 7\\\\ 2 & 5 & 8\\\\ 3 & 6 & 9 \\end{bmatrix} $$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then we transpose the submatrix with corners in cells $$$(2, 2)$$$ and $$$(3, 3)$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$ \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 4 & 7\\\\ 2 & \\textbf{5} & \\textbf{8}\\\\ 3 & \\textbf{6} & \\textbf{9} \\end{bmatrix} $$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So matrix becomes"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$ \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 4 & 7\\\\ 2 & 5 & 6\\\\ 3 & 8 & 9 \\end{bmatrix} $$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"and it is $$$B$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1136C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1136/problem/C"}